      "id": "clai_00317",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Graph network models (CGCNN and MEGNet) have high errors on small datasets (<10^4 samples) but leverage large datasets more efficiently, outperforming traditional ML and AutoML approaches on tasks with approximately 10^4 data points or more."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00321",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Graph networks (CGCNN and MEGNet) far outperform traditional ML algorithms on formation energy prediction tasks, with MEGNet decisively outperforming Automatminer for the PhDOS task; among nine structure-based tasks, Automatminer and MEGNet each achieve best scores on 4 tasks."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00492",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Elemental embedding vectors learned by the crystal formation‑energy MEGNet model reproduce known periodic‑table trends and, when transferred to band‑gap and elastic‑moduli models, reduce their mean absolute errors, improving upon prior machine‑learning approaches."
    },
    {
