      "surface_form": "Graph networks constitute a universal machine‑learning framework that can accurately predict properties for both molecules and crystals."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00557",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "The GNN predicts atomic von Mises stress in polycrystalline graphene with a mean normalized relative error of 5.5% and a maximum error below 7% on a test set of 400 crystals."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00559",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "The GNN reproduces the linear decrease of Young’s modulus with vacancy concentration in porous graphene, matching MD results and yielding the fitted relation E = 823.7 − 5635.6·Cv (GPa)."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00561",
      "type": "claim",
      "surface_form": "Including tensile strain as an input node feature enables the GNN to accurately predict stress evolution during loading, reproducing nonlinear strain‑stress curves for porous graphene."
    },
    {
      "id": "clai_00564",
